{
  "about": "What the videos add to the site. The tutorial runs the site's own tour (src/sightline/tour.json holds its steps and words, and the tour itself puts the screen in each step's state and rings what the step is about); \"acts\" here says where the pointer and the camera go during each step, and that the pointer presses Next at its end. The 30-second demo has words of its own, in its \"script\". record.mjs, beside this file, reads both. In an act, \"at\" and \"until\" are fractions of the step's time (0 is its start, 1 its end), and \"over\" is seconds. \"zoom\" moves the camera in on what it names (\"out\" moves it back to the whole screen, \"frame\" to a part of the screen given as left, top and width); \"max\" is how close it may go. \"intro\" and \"outro\" are the stretches before the first words and after the last.",
